<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Decapolis (Levant)</h1><p class="st-meta">63 BCE – 106 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Decapolis, a group of Greek cities east of the Jordan freed by Pompey, famous for the colonnaded streets of Gerasa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a> cities, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerash">Gerasa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gadara">Gadara</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pella">Pella</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman">Philadelphia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beit-shean">Scythopolis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hippos">Hippos</a>, had grown as Greek-style towns under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hasmonean-kingdom">Hasmonean Kingdom</a> conquered many of them, and in 63 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> freed them and attached them to Roman <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each city governed itself, minted coins and dated years from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey's</a> liberation. They were less a formal league than a regional group with shared Greek culture, temples to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a>, and trade with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nabataean-kingdom">Nabataean Kingdom</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a> mention the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a> as the setting of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>' ministry.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 106 CE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> created the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, dividing the cities between it and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerash">Gerasa</a>, modern Jerash, preserves one of the best-preserved Roman cityscapes.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 63 BCE – 106 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.45%;width:3.36%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>63 BCE – 106 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek, Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Decapolis, Ten Cities</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=22&amp;focus=decapolis-levant" aria-label="Decapolis (Levant) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5622 1047 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Decapolis (Levant) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5942 1303h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5942 1303h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Jordan. <a href="/atlas?year=22&amp;focus=decapolis-levant">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

